  "final_message": "`service2.compute_fee(1000, \"gold\")` returns **480**. Running the function directly gave the same result.\n\nHow it gets there:\n1. `pricing.base_fee(1000)` returns 500 + 1000 // 10 = 600.\n2. `discounts.apply_discount(600, \"gold\")` takes the 20% gold discount: 600 \u2212 (600 \u00d7 20) // 100 = 480.\n\n`decoy_tax.py` (which would add a 25% gold tax) and `decoy_shipping.py` aren't imported by `service2`, so they don't affect the result.\n\nANSWER: 480",
